                                  ABSTRACT
The implementation of tracer studies at Institut Teknologi Kalimantan currently
faces fundamental technical constraints, where questionnaire management in the
existing system remains static with question logic embedded directly into the
program code. This condition results in a high dependency on software developers
whenever changes occur in survey instruments due to the dynamic regulations of
Kemendiktisaintek or specific data needs from study programs. This final project
proposal aims to design and build an adaptive tracer study backend system by
applying the Waterfall Iterative development model and the Repository Design
Pattern architecture. The main design concept focuses on a strict separation
between business logic and the data access layer to improve code readability and
long-term maintenance. The system is developed using the Laravel framework
with Model-View-Controller (MVC) architecture and MySQL database
management, adopting a hybrid relational and JSON structure to accommodate
dynamic forms and branching logic. The implementation method is carried out in
stages, starting from literature study, functional requirement analysis, Unified
Modeling Language (UML) and Business Process Model and Notation (BPMN)
diagram design, to the coding and unit testing phases. Functionally, this
development has the potential to provide independence for the Unit Penunjang
Akademik (UPA) Pengembangan Karier dan Kewirausahaan in managing survey
cycles and question structures in real-time without incurring redevelopment costs.
Furthermore, the system is designed to ensure data interoperability through
RESTful APIs and standardized export features that support reporting to the
Higher Education Database (PDDikti) and BAN-PT accreditation requirements
efficiently and accurately.
Keywords: Tracer Study, Repository Design Pattern, Waterfall Iterative, Backend,
Laravel
